 "description": "Past week's data releases with H.4.1 net liquidity update. Anchored to Friday \u2014 most current when run Friday morning or later. Each release classifies actual vs consensus where BOTH are on file (both Mako-curated): `surprise` is hot / modestly hot / in-line / modestly cool / cool on the headline metric, `vs_consensus` is the same comparison stated neutrally as above/below/in-line, and `metrics` breaks it down per metric. hot/cool is DIRECTIONAL versus consensus, not a verdict \u2014 a hot CPI and a hot payrolls print mean opposite things for the same book. `surprise: \"n/a\"` means the comparison could not be made; `implication` names which half is missing. consensus_provenance.age_days is measured at week_ending, not at call time, so re-asking for an earlier week returns the same age it did the first time.",
